            <value>REFERRAL REQUIRED: Comprehensive Pediatric Eye Examination Needed</value>
          </text>
          <text id="/data/results_refer_group/res_refer_history:label">
            <value>• Risk History: Premature birth, low birth weight, birth defect, systemic disease, or parent concern identified.</value>
          </text>
          <text id="/data/results_refer_group/res_refer_pain:label">
            <value>• Ocular Symptom: Eye pain, discomfort, or severe itchiness reported.</value>
          </text>
          <text id="/data/results_refer_group/res_refer_va:label">
            <value>• Distance Visual Acuity: Reduced vision (&lt; 6/12) in one or both eyes at 3 meters.</value>
          </text>
          <text id="/data/results_refer_group/res_refer_external:label">
            <value>• External Eye Abnormalities detected under ambient light inspection.</value>
          </text>
          <text id="/data/results_refer_group/res_refer_protocol:label">
            <value>Protocol: Refer child to an optometrist, ophthalmic nurse, or ophthalmologist within 30 days. Complete referral form, explain findings to parent/carer, and counsel on hand and eye hygiene.</value>
          </text>
          <text id="/data/results_pass_group:label">
            <value>Results - Screening Passed</value>
          </text>
          <text id="/data/results_pass_group/res_pass_banner:label">
            <value>SCREENING PASSED: Vision and Eye Appearance Within Normal Limits</value>
          </text>
          <text id="/data/results_pass_group/res_pass_counseling:label">
            <value>Child meets visual acuity thresholds (Distance &gt;= 6/12 in each eye for ages 3-5) and no red flags or external abnormalities were observed. Counsel parent/carer on routine follow-up, eye hygiene (hand washing, avoiding eye rubbing), and prompt evaluation if symptoms appear.</value>
